# Story 99: Web Terminal (##rysh web) (50s)
# Hook: Your whole rysh workspace, in a browser tab. One command starts it.
# Duration: 50s
# Source: story-099-web-terminal.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 7

[00:00.0 --> 00:04.0]
Your whole rysh workspace, in a browser tab. One command starts it.

[00:04.0 --> 00:09.0]
Start rysh as usual -- you land in shell mode.

[00:09.0 --> 00:16.0]
Type the rysh-mode command to start the web UI server. With no port, it listens on the default: 23232.

[00:16.0 --> 00:24.0]
Now open your browser to localhost on port 23232. You get the full TUI -- tabs, panes, every input mode -- in the browser.

[00:24.0 --> 00:34.0]
Check the server any time with web status.

[00:34.0 --> 00:42.0]
The browser session shares the same NATS bus and the same actors as your terminal -- it is not a copy, it is the same workspace, live.

[00:42.0 --> 00:50.0]
When you are done, stop it with web stop. One binary, no external dependencies.

